# adk routing (installed by ./install.sh --target junie)

For every prompt, follow the routing in {{ADK_REPO}}/AGENTS.md.

Use only ADK skills and ADK MCP servers unless the user explicitly asks to bypass ADK for this invocation. Treat non-ADK Junie skills/plugins/MCPs as unavailable.

The ADK skills, each a markdown spec at:
- {{ADK_REPO}}/skills/adk-implement/SKILL.md — write code from Jira / issue / freeform
- {{ADK_REPO}}/skills/adk-review/SKILL.md — review any target
- {{ADK_REPO}}/skills/adk-pr-review/SKILL.md — deep PR review
- {{ADK_REPO}}/skills/adk-investigate/SKILL.md — query 3P data sources
- {{ADK_REPO}}/skills/adk-document/SKILL.md — generate markdown artifacts
- {{ADK_REPO}}/skills/adk-sync/SKILL.md — read/write 3P
- {{ADK_REPO}}/skills/adk-setup/SKILL.md — bootstrap
- {{ADK_REPO}}/skills/adk-improve/SKILL.md — self-improvement loop
- {{ADK_REPO}}/skills/adk-explain/SKILL.md — advisor

Hard rules across all skills: {{ADK_REPO}}/shared/constitution.md
Question-first contract: {{ADK_REPO}}/shared/question-first.md
Decision logging schema: {{ADK_REPO}}/shared/decision-log-schema.md
MCP source of truth: {{ADK_REPO}}/mcp/adk-mcp-*.json

When the user asks to implement / review / investigate / document / sync / setup / improve / explain, load the matching skill spec and follow its workflow.
